    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442-a2">

                <pb facs="0580" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg512"/>

                <head>Mr. McCulloch to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-09-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 24, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At the instance of the Light-house Board I
                    have the honor to request that our minister to China be desired to obtain such
                    data in reference to existing aids to navigation on that coast as will enable
                    that board to publish the usual and necessary notices to mariners, and that he
                    also communicate the number of Americans appointed to carry out the cosmopolitan
                    system of Mr. Hart, inspector generai of customs.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. McCULLOCH, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                        Treasury</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
